---
import { marked } from 'marked';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../styles/global.css';
import markdown from '../content/README.md?raw';
// The README's own leading block (logo image, centered title, tagline, nav links, up to the
// first `---`) duplicates what the hand-built hero above already shows, including an <img
// src="assets/logo.svg"> that 404s once served from the site root. Render only what follows the
// first horizontal rule on the page; the "Copy as Markdown"/.md endpoint still serve the full,
// untrimmed README verbatim.
const bodyMarkdown = markdown.split(/^---$/m).slice(1).join('\n---\n') || markdown;
const html = marked.parse(bodyMarkdown);
---
<Layout description="Djangors is a batteries-included web framework for Rust: the ORM, migrations, admin site, forms, auth, a REST framework, background tasks, payments, and multi-tenancy. Everything that makes Django pleasant, with Rust's speed, safety, and single-binary deploys."><section class="hero"><h1>The Django of Rust.</h1><p class="lede">Everything that makes Django pleasant: the ORM, migrations, the admin, forms, auth, the batteries, the docs, the tutorial. All of it with Rust's speed, safety, and single-binary deploys.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="https://github.com/Chidi09/djangors">View on GitHub ↗</a><a class="outline" href="/docs/">Read the docs</a></div></section><section class="pillars"><div class="pillar"><h3>Compile-time safety</h3><p>A typo'd field name or a wrong type passed to a query is a build failure, not a bug found in production. The ORM's query builder, model metadata, and form validation are all checked by <code>rustc</code> before the code ships.</p></div><div class="pillar"><h3>Actually fast</h3><p>No GIL, no GC pauses. Djangors runs on Tokio's async runtime, and it's backed by honest <code>oha</code>-driven HTTP benchmarks against Django/Gunicorn and axum, not marketing numbers.</p><a href="/benchmarks">See the benchmarks &rarr;</a></div><div class="pillar"><h3>Secure by default</h3><p>CSRF protection, security headers, HSTS, a CSP builder, and HttpOnly signed sessions ship enabled out of the box, backed by a real internal security review.</p><a href="/docs/guides/security.html">Read the security guide &rarr;</a></div></section><section class="get-started"><h2>Get started</h2><div class="get-started-grid"><a class="get-started-card" href="https://github.com/Chidi09/djangors#quick-start"><h3>Install Djangors</h3><p>Clone the repo, scaffold a new project with the <code>dj</code> CLI, and have a running server in minutes.</p></a><a class="get-started-card" href="/docs/tutorial/01-requests-and-responses.html"><h3>Follow the tutorial</h3><p>The real, verified 8-part tutorial builds the same polls app Django's own tutorial does, using this exact codebase's real APIs.</p></a></div></section><section class="features"><h2>What's included</h2><div class="features-grid"><a class="feature-card" href="/docs/guides/orm.html"><h3>ORM</h3><p><code>QuerySet</code>, filter/order/aggregate expressions, and race-safe bulk operations.</p></a><a class="feature-card" href="/docs/guides/admin.html"><h3>Admin site</h3><p>An auto-generated changelist, filters, bulk actions, and a full audit log.</p></a><a class="feature-card" href="/docs/guides/auth.html"><h3>Auth</h3><p>Argon2id password hashing, login rate limiting, and persistent account lockout.</p></a><a class="feature-card" href="/docs/guides/payments.html"><h3>Payments</h3><p>A Paystack integration with idempotent, database-constraint-backed transaction recording.</p></a><a class="feature-card" href="/docs/guides/multi-tenancy.html"><h3>Multi-tenancy</h3><p>Membership-verified per-request tenant scoping that reuses the REST framework's own enforcement.</p></a><a class="feature-card" href="/docs/guides/deployment.html"><h3>Deployment</h3><p><code>dj deploy</code> ships to Render or any VPS over SSH, straight from the CLI.</p></a><a class="feature-card" href="/docs/guides/pdf.html"><h3>PDF generation</h3><p>A typed, pure-Rust builder for report cards, invoices, and receipts. No headless browser required.</p></a><a class="feature-card" href="/docs/guides/settings.html"><h3>Typed settings</h3><p>Validated app configuration loaded from environment variables, checked at startup, not at runtime.</p></a></div></section><article class="markdown"><button class="copy" data-markdown={markdown}>Copy as Markdown</button><Fragment set:html={html} /></article></Layout>
